Once the groundwork is laid in bug 1874936 and 1874934, we need to actually support the co-enrolling logic and new merged values.

* Enrollment gating occurs in [`ExperimentManager#enroll`](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/2fa4750e87d49ec7ad19fa1da167a03ef6d5e954/toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/ExperimentManager.sys.mjs#408-414). The logic has to be updated to ensure that we ignore features that specify `allow-coenrollment: true`.
* [`getVariable()`](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/ae3df68e9ba2faeaf76445a7650e4e742eb7b4e7/toolkit/components/nimbus/ExperimentAPI.sys.mjs#386) and [`getAllVariables()`](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/ae3df68e9ba2faeaf76445a7650e4e742eb7b4e7/toolkit/components/nimbus/ExperimentAPI.sys.mjs#361) need to be updated to support the new algorithm. A sketch of each in pseudocode follows:

```
function getVariable(variable) {
  if (this.allowCoenrollment) {
    return this.getAllVariables()[variable];
  } else {
    // current getvariable impl
  }
}

function getAllVariables() {
  if (this.allowCoenrollment) {
    return jsonMergePatch(
      this.fallbackPrefs,
      ...rolloutValues,
      ...experimentValues,
  } else {
    // current getAllVariables impl
  }
}
```

The merged values should be in the order (from first applied to last applied):
* the default values (ie fallback prefs)
* the value of each rollout in order of enrollment (oldest first)
* the value of each experiment in order of enrollment (oldest first)

That is, a newly enrolled experiment will override values from previously enrolled experiments.

